-- title:
--   Kronecker congruence in Gauss form for X₁(Mp) chart functions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 1$, a field $L$ of characteristic zero that is a $p$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, and a unit $\zeta \in L^{\times}$ whose underlying element is a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, acting on $K$ compatibly with $L$; let $j \in K$ have $q$-expansion the coefficientwise image of the $j$-series, and $j \neq 0$. Assume $q \mapsto q^p$ carries the function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ into the field $x1x0FunctionFieldC$ at levels $(Mp, Mp\cdot p)$, and that the associated $L$-algebra map `heckeBetaOneBar` has degree $p$. Write $R$ for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$. Then for every $g \in R$ there is a monic $E \in R[X]$ of degree $p$ whose coefficients, pushed to $L((q))$ and then substituted $q \mapsto q^p$ (exponents multiplied by $p$), satisfy $E = \prod_{i=0}^{p-1}\bigl(X - C(g(\zeta^{i}q))\bigr)$, where $g(\zeta^{i}q)$ is the twist multiplying the $k$-th coefficient by $\zeta^{ik}$; moreover each coefficient $E_k$ with $0 < k < p$, and also $E_0 - (-1)^p g$, is a quotient $x/y$ in the sense that its image in $L((q))$ times the series attached to $y$ equals that attached to $x$, for some $x, y \in A[[q]]$ with $y$ nonzero and $x$ zero modulo the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This is Kronecker's congruence $\prod_i (X - g(\zeta^i q)) \equiv X^p - g(q^p) \pmod{\mathfrak{m}_A}$, transported from the classical modular polynomial $\Phi_p$ to an arbitrary function on the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ over a cyclotomic discrete valuation ring, with the congruence expressed in Gauss form (numerator and denominator in $A[[q]]$). It feeds the construction of the Hecke divisor on the two-chart and Igusa models of $X_1(Mp)$ and the identification of the reduction of $\beta$-conjugates with a Frobenius twist.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_exists_monic_map_eq_prod_X_sub_C_qTwist_and_gaussPresentation_chartAlgFin_x1_mul.lean

